---
/**
 * Terms of use — DRAFT (compliance scope, CLAUDE.md).
 *
 * Status: DRAFT — placeholders in [BRACKETS] must be completed by the operator
 * and the whole page MUST be reviewed by a qualified lawyer before launch
 * (CLAUDE.md: terms are draft-only until human lawyer review). The "not legal
 * advice" framing is core to this product's risk posture — do not soften it.
 * Do NOT remove the draft banner until lawyer sign-off is recorded in DECISIONS.md.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const linkClass =
  'text-link underline hover:text-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent rounded';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use — Relocation Guide"
  description="The terms governing your use of Relocation Guide. Informational only — not legal or immigration advice."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px]">
    <!-- DRAFT banner — remove only after human lawyer sign-off -->
    <aside
      role="note"
      aria-label="Draft status"
      class="rounded-field border border-warning-border bg-warning-soft p-4 text-sm text-warning"
    >
      <p>
        <strong class="font-semibold">DRAFT — not yet in force.</strong> These terms contain
        placeholder values in [BRACKETS] and have not been reviewed by a lawyer. They must not
        be relied upon as a binding agreement until the operator details are completed and a
        qualified lawyer has approved them.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <article class="mt-10 space-y-12">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Terms of use</h1>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          These terms govern your use of Relocation Guide (the "site"), operated by
          [OPERATOR NAME]. By using the site you agree to them. If you do not agree, please
          do not use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">
          Information only — not legal advice
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          The site provides general, educational information about relocating between
          countries.
          <strong class="font-semibold text-label">
            It is not legal, immigration, tax, or financial advice</strong>, and using it does
          not create any advisory, client, or professional relationship. We are not a law firm
          and not licensed immigration advisers. Always confirm your situation with the relevant
          official authority or a licensed adviser before acting.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">
          Accuracy and official sources
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          We work hard to trace each factual claim to an official source, to have it checked
          by a separate reviewer, and to show you the source and the date it was last
          verified. Even so, immigration rules change frequently and may change between our
          last check and your reading. The official authority's current rules always take
          precedence over anything on this site. Where we could not confirm a detail, we say
          so and point you to the authority to confirm.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">External links and forms</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          The site links to official authorities and third-party services so you can obtain
          and submit official forms directly. We do not control those sites and are not
          responsible for their content, availability, or processing of your data. We never
          host official government forms ourselves &mdash; always obtain them from the issuing
          authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          <li>Use the site for your own lawful, personal relocation planning.</li>
          <li>Do not misuse the site, attempt to disrupt it, or scrape it at scale.</li>
          <li>
            Do not reproduce substantial parts of the content commercially without
            permission. [Confirm licensing intent with counsel.]
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">No warranty</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind to
          the extent permitted by law, including as to accuracy, completeness, or fitness for
          a particular purpose. [Lawyer to tailor warranty disclaimer to each jurisdiction;
          consumer-protection law may limit exclusions.]
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss arising from
          decisions you make based on the site. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that
          cannot lawfully be excluded (for example, for death or personal injury caused by
          negligence, or for fraud). [Lawyer to set the precise limitation, which differs by
          jurisdiction and for consumers.]
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Changes</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          We may update the site and these terms from time to time. Continued use after a
          change means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          These terms are governed by the laws of [JURISDICTION], without prejudice to any
          mandatory consumer-protection rights you have where you live. [Lawyer to confirm
          governing law and venue, accounting for EU/Swiss consumer rules.]
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-label">Contact</h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed text-secondaryLabel">
          Questions about these terms: [CONTACT EMAIL]. Operator details are in our
          <a href="/impressum" class={linkClass}>Impressum</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-sm text-tertiaryLabel">
        Last updated: [DATE — set when placeholders are filled in]. Draft pending human
        lawyer review.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
